{"schema": 1, "kind": "review", "id": "rev-20261030T031143Z-79145506", "ts": "2026-10-30T03:15:03Z", "actor": {"worktree": "prawduct", "plugin": "3.8.0-dev.2", "branch": "fix/clear-gate-telemetry", "build": "48a80398de30"}, "body": {"base_commit": "48a80398de30807018366c32d711af1eaab52aca", "base_tree": "76be4a53b25b0a636dd85b54c58132981bf0c3f7", "head_tree": "ee0504284f676add12a45400fadfdea11ba15f8b", "head_commit": "30857ac89d591dd834745e7410566591a9c43c58", "dispatch_commit": "30857ac89d591dd834745e7410566591a9c43c58", "mode": "cumulative (bundle review, ready for merge)", "mode_chosen_by": "explicit-args", "stage": "boundary", "tier": "escalate", "roster": [{"role": "correctness", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}, {"role": "design", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}, {"role": "sustainability", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}], "files_reviewed": ["plugin/bin/prawduct-hook", "plugin/docs/governance-telemetry.md", "plugin/lib/evidence.py", "plugin/lib/gates.py", "plugin/lib/standing_block.py", "plugin/lib/stats.py", "plugin/methodology/session-digest.md", "plugin/methodology/session-hygiene.md", "tests/test_stats.py", "tests/test_stop_block_facts.py", "tests/test_stop_verdict_defer.py", "tests/test_v5_methodology.py"], "files_changed": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-clear-gate-telemetry.md", ".prawduct/changes/clear-gate-telemetry.md", "plugin/bin/prawduct-hook", "plugin/docs/governance-telemetry.md", "plugin/lib/evidence.py", "plugin/lib/gates.py", "plugin/lib/standing_block.py", "plugin/lib/stats.py", "plugin/methodology/session-digest.md", "plugin/methodology/session-hygiene.md", "tests/test_stats.py", "tests/test_stop_block_facts.py", "tests/test_stop_verdict_defer.py", "tests/test_v5_methodology.py"], "files_oracle": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-clear-gate-telemetry.md", ".prawduct/changes/clear-gate-telemetry.md"], "findings": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Unintended", "severity": "warning", "title": "work_live is now the clear-verdict gate's authority input, but its waiver and docstring still call it advice that never changes a Stop's verdict", "recommendation": "In Chunk 02, cmd_stop lets `YOUR TURN` + `DO NOT CLEAR` through exactly when `_clear_observations(...)[work_live] is True`. That observation now decides the verdict. The broad-except waiver on the `work_live` try block still gives the reason 'an observation is advice; it must never change a Stop's verdict', which is no longer true. The function's docstring also still describes it only as input for the reader that tells a catch from a slip (`stats`). Today the failure path returns None and the gate blocks (fails closed), so the behaviour is correct. The risk is a maintainer who trusts the waiver: they could make `work_live` softer (count something unobservable as live, or treat an unreadable marker as True) and silently widen an authority gate. Waiver reasons must be genuine (Goal 3). Fix: give the work_live waiver a true reason, for example that an unreadable observation is None and the clear-verdict gate blocks on anything but True. Have the docstring name cmd_stop's clear-verdict gate as a consumer that fails closed. Scope: instance. The session_changed and notes_present waivers are still advice-only and are fine. The matching 'Asks only, to record what a clear gate saw' comment in tests/test_critic_session_guard.py (its seam table) is the same instance.", "files": ["plugin/bin/prawduct-hook"], "fid": "R-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "severity": "warning", "title": "Records describing the old invariant ('only RUNNING may say DO NOT CLEAR', YOUR TURN + DNC refused) and citing the renamed pin test were not updated", "recommendation": "The core rule 'A mechanism change is done when every artifact DESCRIBING it agrees' applies here. A search of the claim at HEAD (`git grep \"only \\`RUNNING\\` may\\|test_only_running_may_say\"`) finds two stale records. (1) The 'Session continuity across /clear' row in .prawduct/cross-cutting-concerns.md (line 55) says 'only `RUNNING` may say `DO NOT CLEAR`' and that the clear-verdict gate 'refuses `YOUR TURN`/`COMPLETE` + `DO NOT CLEAR`'. It also cites `test_only_running_may_say_do_not_clear_on_every_carrier` as the pin, but this diff renamed that test to `test_do_not_clear_needs_work_a_clear_would_kill_on_every_carrier`. (2) Row A14 in .prawduct/artifacts/digest-behavior-inventory.md still states the retired rule and its RUNNING-only remedy. The registry is what the Critic and pipeline-coverage readers use to judge whether a concern is covered. A maintainer would believe the pair is still refused everywhere and would look for a pin that no longer exists. Fix: update both rows to the narrowed rule (COMPLETE never; YOUR TURN only while the hook observes work a clear would kill) and update the test citation. Leave dated archive and CHANGELOG entries alone. Scope: instance (two sites, found by searching for the claim).", "files": [".prawduct/cross-cutting-concerns.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/digest-behavior-inventory.md"], "fid": "R-2"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "severity": "note", "title": "The live-review YOUR TURN test passes vacuously if the hook crashes", "recommendation": "`test_your_turn_beside_a_live_review_stands` asserts only that 'CLEAR VERDICT' is absent from stderr. It does not check the return code (another gate may block in this fixture), so a traceback or an early return would also pass. The background-task sibling does assert returncode 0. Add a positive control: assert there is no 'Traceback' in stderr, and either assert the exact return code this fixture produces or assert that the blocked section names some other gate but not `gate: clear-verdict`. Scope: instance.", "files": ["tests/test_stop_verdict_defer.py"], "fid": "R-3"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "severity": "warning", "title": "Sweep incomplete: four surfaces still describe the old 'only RUNNING may say DO NOT CLEAR' rule", "recommendation": "Core learning 'A mechanism change is done when every artifact DESCRIBING it agrees: search for the claim, not the tokens you edited'. Chunk 02 narrowed clear-verdict so that YOUR TURN + DO NOT CLEAR passes when work_live is observed, but four places still state the old rule. (1) plugin/hooks/gates.json:56, the clear-verdict registry `summary`: \"`DO NOT CLEAR` belongs only to a `RUNNING` turn\". This is the shipped description of the gate. (2) plugin/lib/gates.py:985-990, the turn_declares_in_flight docstring: a handed-over turn \"owes `SAFE TO CLEAR` ... the Stop hook refuses that pairing outright\". This is a subject file; the docstring for turn_contradicts_its_verdict was updated three functions below, but this one was not. (3) .prawduct/artifacts/digest-behavior-inventory.md A14, \"Only RUNNING may say DO NOT CLEAR\", with the expected behaviour 'with a live review it closes RUNNING + DO NOT CLEAR'. (4) .prawduct/artifacts/nonfunctional-requirements.md:47, which says clear-verdict \"refuses a turn closing `YOUR TURN` or `COMPLETE` with `DO NOT CLEAR`\". Fix: change each to the narrowed rule (COMPLETE + DO NOT CLEAR is always refused; YOUR TURN + DO NOT CLEAR is refused unless background work or a live review is observed). Also consider recording the retired wording in the change fragment so that record_lint's retired-claim-survives check owns the next sweep.", "files": ["plugin/hooks/gates.json", "plugin/lib/gates.py", ".prawduct/artifacts/digest-behavior-inventory.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/nonfunctional-requirements.md"], "fid": "R-4"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "severity": "warning", "title": "governance-telemetry's clear-verdict verdict rule does not say the narrowing removed its slip population", "recommendation": "plugin/docs/governance-telemetry.md (the 'clear-verdict is a slip when work_live' bullet) is unchanged. Before Chunk 02, a YOUR TURN + DO NOT CLEAR firing with work_live True was recorded and counted as a slip; the plan puts that at 7 of the 10 3.8 firings. That case no longer fires, so it is never recorded. From now on, a clear-verdict slip can only come from COMPLETE, and every YOUR TURN firing has work_live False or None, which counts as catch or unclassified. Over a window that spans the release, stats will show clear-verdict's catch share jumping. The gate did not get more accurate: its passes stopped being recorded. The plan says #1044 decides on exactly this data. That gives a concrete wrong action: someone reading the catch rate concludes the gate earns its keep. Fix: add one sentence to that bullet saying YOUR TURN firings with observed live work stopped being recorded at this release, so slip counts before and after it are not comparable. It could also give the release or a date to bound windows by. Recording passes is the alternative if the data must stay comparable.", "files": ["plugin/docs/governance-telemetry.md"], "fid": "R-5"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "severity": "note", "title": "session-hygiene Precedence names a case the hook refuses, an unreaped delegate, as YOUR TURN + DO NOT CLEAR", "recommendation": "Precedence (session-hygiene.md:32) gives 'a live review, an unreaped delegate' as the work for which 'YOUR TURN + DO NOT CLEAR' is right. Two paragraphs later (line 39), the doc says the hook cannot see an unread delegate's finished output and tells you to close that RUNNING. Following Precedence for a finished but unread delegate gets refused, and the clear-verdict block text then says 'this hook sees nothing a clear would kill'. That costs one round trip, and the later paragraph reconciles it, so this is prose at the NOTE ceiling. If line 32 is touched again anyway, it could say 'a live review or running background work' and send the unread-output case to RUNNING in the same sentence. No dedicated edit is wanted.", "files": ["plugin/methodology/session-hygiene.md"], "fid": "R-6"}, {"goal": "The System Can Be Understood", "severity": "warning", "title": "The retired 'only RUNNING may say DO NOT CLEAR' invariant and the renamed test survive in three records outside the diff", "recommendation": "Class. Why it broke: the change rewrote the invariant on the two carriers it pins (session-hygiene.md, session-digest.md) and renamed its test, but never searched for the claim elsewhere. That breaks the core rule 'A mechanism change is done when every artifact DESCRIBING it agrees: search for the claim, not the tokens you edited...'. Three survivors on HEAD: (1) .prawduct/cross-cutting-concerns.md, the 'Session continuity across /clear' row, says in the present tense that 'only `RUNNING` may say `DO NOT CLEAR`' and that the gate 'refuses `YOUR TURN`/`COMPLETE` + `DO NOT CLEAR`'. It also cites `test_only_running_may_say_do_not_clear_on_every_carrier`, which this diff renamed to `test_do_not_clear_needs_work_a_clear_would_kill_on_every_carrier`, so the citation now points at nothing. (2) .prawduct/artifacts/digest-behavior-inventory.md row A14 is titled 'Only RUNNING may say DO NOT CLEAR', and it says the Stop hook 'refuses the pair'. A judge grading a turn against this inventory would fail a `YOUR TURN` + `DO NOT CLEAR` close beside a live review, which is now legal. (3) .prawduct/artifacts/nonfunctional-requirements.md:47 says the gate 'refuses a turn closing `YOUR TURN` or `COMPLETE` with `DO NOT CLEAR`'. Remedy by construction, not by a longer list: a deterministic enforcer already exists (`retired-claim-survives`, lib/retired_claims.py), but this change declared no `Retires:` field. Add `Retires:` to .prawduct/changes/clear-gate-telemetry.md with the quoted phrasings ('Only `RUNNING` may say `DO NOT CLEAR`', 'test_only_running_may_say_do_not_clear_on_every_carrier'). record_lint will then list every survivor, including any beyond these three. Make each survivor relational or delete it; don't reword the narration.", "files": ["plugin/methodology/session-hygiene.md", "tests/test_v5_methodology.py"], "fid": "R-7"}, {"goal": "The System Can Be Understood", "severity": "note", "title": "session_changed records False when session_work_span degraded to porcelain and could not see committed work", "recommendation": "Instance. `_clear_observations` stores `bool(session_work_span(...)['changed'])` and drops `source`. session_work_span's docstring says a caller owes 'the difference between \"nothing changed\" and \"this reader could not tell\"'. On `source == 'porcelain'` (marker missing or malformed) committed work is invisible, so a session that committed everything records `session_changed: False`. The function's own docstring promises `None` there. The stats verdict is unaffected, because catch needs True and False and None both read as unclassified. Only the stored fact is less honest than its contract, so this is a NOTE. If you touch it, record None when `source != 'base-tree'` and `changed` is empty.", "files": ["plugin/bin/prawduct-hook"], "fid": "R-8"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "note", "title": "Mid-build decisions and their settlement, for the owner", "recommendation": "Scope none. Decision (a): a read-only session's clear-reason firing is unclassified, not a slip. Settled by Honest Confidence and recorded in the plan's 'Decisions made mid-build'. Decision (b): the YOUR TURN narrowing passes only when the observation is True; None and unobservable delegates still block. Settled by architecture.md 'Authority fails closed; advice fails soft', recorded under Norm reconciliation and in the hook comment. Decision (c): narrow clear-verdict now rather than wait for #1044's quarter of data. This is an owner ruling, recorded in Goals. Alignment-pass miss: none found. Goals are stated and not hedged, and every capability traces to the plan's Problem section and has a consumer: `session_changed` is read by `stats.CATCH_REQUIRES_OBSERVED`, and the narrowing by cmd_stop. Related core rule: 'A governance change cannot supply its own authority...'. The amendment to the session-hygiene norm rests on an owner 'yes to all' that is recorded only in this branch's agent-authored plan and fragment. Linking the owner's own words, or the #1044 comment the plan promised, would put that authority somewhere the amendment isn't.", "fid": "R-9"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "note", "title": "Learnings Cross-Check: one regression class found, no corpus supersession, no rules changed this cycle", "recommendation": "Scope none. I read core.md, authoring.md, gates.md, hook-surface.md, release.md and tests.md (the `learnings-files --for-diff` list). One rule fired: core 'A mechanism change is done when every artifact DESCRIBING it agrees'. It is filed as the WARNING above and not repeated here. I checked hook-surface 'When a change redefines a FIELD, enumerate its READERS' against clear-verdict's narrowed meaning. Its only verdict reader (stats.SLIP_WHEN_OBSERVED) still holds, because a YOUR TURN firing with work_live True no longer occurs and a COMPLETE one is still a slip. This diff adds or edits no learnings rule, and I found no implicit supersession.", "fid": "R-10"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "note", "title": "Backlog Reconciliation: no open item resolved; #1044 is open in the touched area", "recommendation": "Scope none. `cache-query affecting` (cache 1h old) returns #672 and #928, and this change resolves neither. C-B3: #1044 ('decide if clear-verdict and clear-reason earn their cost') is open, and this change re-derives its data: clear-reason catches now need session_changed, and clear-verdict no longer fires on YOUR TURN beside observed work. Update #1044 with both changes. The plan's Goals already promised 'comment the classifier point on #1044'; verify that comment exists. Without it, whoever reads clear-verdict's firing rate across this release sees a drop and may read it as the gate getting more accurate, when the gate actually fires on fewer cases. #932 is already shipped. Keep it shipped, but the comment on #1044 could mention that this change partly narrows #932's fix.", "fid": "R-11"}], "counts": {"blocking": 0, "warning": 5, "note": 6}, "observations": [], "duration_seconds": 420, "scope": "clear-gate-telemetry", "scope_chosen_by": "binding", "scope_unresolved_cause": null, "scope_reason": null, "base_extended_from": null, "chunks": ["01", "02"], "chunks_proposed": ["01", "02"], "chunk": "01", "base_reviewed": "48a80398de30807018366c32d711af1eaab52aca", "record_lint": {"records": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-clear-gate-telemetry.md", ".prawduct/changes/clear-gate-telemetry.md", "plugin/docs/governance-telemetry.md", "plugin/methodology/session-digest.md", "plugin/methodology/session-hygiene.md"], "chunk_graded": "01", "chunks_graded": ["01", "02"], "plan_graded": ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-clear-gate-telemetry.md", "findings": [{"check": "governed-by-gap", "path": ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-clear-gate-telemetry.md", "line": 10, "detail": ".prawduct/artifacts/architecture.md carries 8 `## Direction` norm(s) but this plan disposes of 0 \u2014 each norm needs a recorded disposition, and \"inapplicable, because \u2014\" is one (a bare path holds none: write it as `- artifact: <name>` with `dispositions:`)"}, {"check": "governed-by-gap", "path": ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-clear-gate-telemetry.md", "line": 11, "detail": ".prawduct/artifacts/api-contract.md carries 3 `## Direction` norm(s) but this plan disposes of 0 \u2014 each norm needs a recorded disposition, and \"inapplicable, because \u2014\" is one (a bare path holds none: write it as `- artifact: <name>` with `dispositions:`)"}], "unchecked": [], "counts": {"chunk-ref-missing": 0, "governed-by-gap": 2, "suite-total-claim": 0, "learnings-over-budget": 0, "learnings-budget-unreasoned": 0, "learnings-core-raise-unapproved": 0, "learnings-rule-too-long": 0, "learnings-rule-body": 0, "learnings-area-dead": 0, "change-fragment": 0, "retired-claim-survives": 0}}, "dispatched_at": "2026-10-30T03:11:45Z"}}

